MECHANICS
==========

> Classes

	> Martial
	> Spellcaster

> Each character level provides a point to put in any stat
> Stats: 
	> Strength 
	> Agility
	> Constitution
	> Intelligence
	> Wisdom

> Player cant pass a specified level cap at each difficulty area (exponential?)
> Enemy stats scales to area difficulty (assigned to towns)
> Dungeon Mechanic, location on the map, more levels are acsessable in higher difficulty areas
	> Player cant acsess the deeper levels until they reach certain stats/levels
> Doing things provides minor exp for a stat level, but provides major exp towards charater level

	> Fighting
		> Major exp is the individual monster exp value
		> If fight ends early, minor exp = (monster exp value / 3) - (the remaining health of the enemy as a percentage)
		> Provides minor exp to Strength = (monster exp value / 3)
		> If class is spellcaster provides minor exp to Intelligence instead of strength = (monster exp value / 3)

		> Checks for class
			> loop, while (player != dead or run) or (enemy != dead or run)
			> Introduces enemy name and health
			> Offers the class appropriate heal and attack option or option to run
				> If option = heal
					> 


	> Foraging / Fishing
		> Major exp = forage item exp value
		> Minor exp = (forage item exp value / 3)
		> Random split of minor exp provided to Dexterity and Wisdom
	
	> Hunting
		> Major exp = hunting target exp value (based on animal rarity or exp value)
		> Minor exp = (hunting target exp value / 3)
		> Minor exp is split randomly between Dexterity and Wisdom (weighted towards dexterity)

	> Cooking
		> Major exp = combined food cook exp value (perhaps the health it provides)
		> Minor exp = Wisdom level / 10
		> Minor exp is split randomly between Intelligence and Wisdom (weighted towards Wisdom)



